{
  "esm": "0.7.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "USGS3DEP_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) terrain elevation at ~1/3 arc-second (~10 m) resolution. Provides static (time-invariant) terrain elevation and the two runtime-derived slope components (dzdx, dzdy) on a geographic (longlat/WGS84, EPSG:4326) lattice, sourced from the USGS National Map ImageServer REST API as a GeoTIFF cropped to the model domain.\n\nThis is the loader half of the usgs3dep loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.4). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads/derives (with units), and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/usgs3dep.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./usgs3dep_loader.esm\"}.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (EPSG:4326 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (usgs3dep.esm `regrid`). This is a STATIC (time-invariant) dataset: there is NO `temporal` block, so the loader seeds CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5) — the runtime fetches the GeoTIFF once per simulation domain and never refreshes it (kind: static). Cadence derives from the absence of `temporal`, orthogonal to the `kind` enum.\n\nSlope components (dzdx, dzdy) are derived from the elevation field at runtime by finite differences (all three variables share file_variable 'elevation'); the metric constants are documented in metadata.slope_derivation.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:326 (USGS3DEPFileSet, USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet, USGS3DEP constructor). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/usgs3dep.esm (esm-tibb).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "elevation",
      "terrain",
      "slope",
      "static",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "usgs3dep",
      "dem",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.4)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "U.S. Geological Survey. 3D Elevation Program (3DEP). National Map Elevation Imagery Service. https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/",
        "url": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:1-410 (USGS3DEPFileSet, USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet, USGS3DEP constructor). Test: test/usgs3dep_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "USGS3DEP_data": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/3DEPElevation/ImageServer/exportImage?bbox={bbox_west},{bbox_south},{bbox_east},{bbox_north}&size={width},{height}&format=tiff&bboxSR=4326&imageSR=4326&pixelType=F32&interpolation=+RSP_BilinearInterpolation&f=image"
      },
      "grid": {
        "family": "cartesian",
        "crs": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84"
        },
        "description": "Native USGS 3DEP grid: regular geographic (longlat/WGS84, EPSG:4326) lattice at ~1/3 arc-second (~10 m, 0.00009259°) resolution. Geographic (unprojected) crs — the regridding model applies the longlat identity reprojection (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. The bounding box and cell counts are domain-derived at load time: the GeoTIFF is requested at the WGS84 envelope of the model domain, so lon/lat cell counts (n_lon, n_lat) are resolved from the source response at load time and capped at 1000×1000 pixels per request. The documented native cell size is 0.00009259° in both lon and lat; US coverage is lon ∈ [-180°, -60°], lat ∈ [17°, 72°] (CONUS + Alaska + Hawaii + US territories); cells outside US territory return NaN.",
        "dimensions": [
          "lon",
          "lat"
        ],
        "extents": {
          "lon": {
            "n": "n_lon",
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lat": {
            "n": "n_lat",
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        },
        "parameters": {
          "n_lon": {
            "units": "1",
            "description": "Longitude cell count, resolved from the source GeoTIFF at load time. Domain-derived: width = min(1000, round((bbox_east - bbox_west) / 0.00009259))."
          },
          "n_lat": {
            "units": "1",
            "description": "Latitude cell count, resolved from the source GeoTIFF at load time. Domain-derived: height = min(1000, round((bbox_north - bbox_south) / 0.00009259))."
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "elevation": {
          "file_variable": "Band1",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Terrain elevation above WGS84 ellipsoid (m). Fetched directly from the USGS 3DEP ImageServer GeoTIFF response — a single-band raster, so the GeoTIFF reader keys it 'Band1'. No-data pixels outside US territory are NaN. The slope components dzdx/dzdy are NOT loaded here: this loader is pure I/O, and the slopes are derived declaratively from this elevation field by grad equations in the regridding model (usgs3dep.esm)."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "U.S. Geological Survey. 3D Elevation Program (3DEP). National Map Elevation Imagery Service. https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/",
        "url": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": ["elevation", "terrain", "slope", "static", "derived", "usgs3dep", "longlat"],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/usgs3dep.jl::USGS3DEPFileSet, src/usgs3dep.jl::USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet",
        "native_crs_epsg": "EPSG:4326 (geographic longlat / WGS84 — encoded as crs {projection: longlat, datum: WGS84})",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "lon": 0.00009259,
          "lat": 0.00009259
        },
        "native_staggering": "Cell-centered (lon 'center', lat 'center') — 3DEP is a regular non-staggered raster. The regridding model regrids elevation conservatively (RFC §5.2; bead esm-3nc.4 cell-centered → conservative); see usgs3dep.esm regrid. The slopes dzdx/dzdy are model-derived (grad of the regridded elevation), not loaded.",
        "native_extent": {
          "lon": [-180.0, -60.0],
          "lat": [17.0, 72.0]
        },
        "resolution_arc_seconds": 0.333,
        "coverage": "US only (CONUS + Alaska + Hawaii + US territories). Cells outside US territory return NaN.",
        "url_substitutions": "bbox_{west,south,east,north} are domain bounding box in decimal degrees (WGS84); {width} and {height} are pixel dimensions capped at 1000 (= min(1000, round((E-W)/resolution)) and min(1000, round((N-S)/resolution)) respectively)",
        "url_defaults": {"size_cap": 1000},
        "max_request_pixels": "1000x1000",
        "file_format": "GeoTIFF (F32 pixel type)",
        "slope_derivation": "Slope components dzdx/dzdy are derived declaratively in the regridding model usgs3dep.esm as grad(elevation, x|y) over the regridded elevation field — they are NOT loaded here. This loader exposes only the single-band elevation GeoTIFF (GDAL band 'Band1'). On a projected/metric target grid the gradient is already m/m, so no lon/lat metre correction is needed.",
        "static_note": "No temporal block: kind='static' and the absence of `temporal` seed CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5). The runtime fetches the GeoTIFF once per simulation domain. Upstream DataFrequencyInfo uses two bracketing time points solely to satisfy the interp_unsafe interface; no time interpolation occurs."
      }
    }
  }
}
